1
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:08,780
This arrow is irreplaceable.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,588
There's only one, you know.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,837
It's essential to my mission.

4
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:15,120
And losing it is not an option.

5
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:19,000
Hey, leave that arrow alone!

6
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:21,160
He'll bleed out if you keep it up!

7
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:25,644
Because of the failings
of my blockhead brother,

8
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,329
I now have no other
choice but to kill you.

9
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,457
Nothing personal, but I can't
let anything happen to the arrow.

10
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:36,422
It wouldn't do for it to break or
catch the eye of some old crone.

11
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,200
Given my meticulous nature,

12
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,897
I feel somewhat compelled to
return it to its proper place.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:46,862
I mean, what should one do when
one is finished listening to a CD?

14
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:50,697
You should put the first in its
case before listening to the next.

15
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:52,427
That's how everyone does it.

16
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:54,360
And it's how I do things.

17
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:58,480
Now what's this?

18
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,957
So you've decided to enter our abode.

19
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:02,320
No shit, Sherlock!

20
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:07,208
How else was I supposed to beat your
smarmy ass and get Koichi back to normal?

21
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,290
Hm.

22
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:09,490
Brother!

23
00:01:09,573 --> 00:01:11,147
Don't count me out just yet!

24
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:14,460
Wait for me to help before
you attack him! Attack?

25
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:16,060
I hope you're ready!

26
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:18,680
This fight is just getting started!

27
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:21,457
There's something moving
up there in the dark.

28
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:22,480
What the hell?

29
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:54,340
GASP

30
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:32,640
But today I'm going to be a
little bit more than a day.

31
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:39,020
I'm going to be a little
bit more crazy noise.

32
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:46,520
I'm going to be a little bit more.

33
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:58,050
Okuyasu!

34
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:00,760
Your stupidity is truly astounding.

35
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:04,618
If you hadn't stumbled in
here like a bumbling idiot,

36
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:07,577
worse company would have
already destroyed Josuke.

37
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:10,954
And what's more, you walked
right into the line of fire.

38
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:14,297
But bro, I...

39
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:19,140
Your stand, the hand, may be menacing,
but you, little brother, are a fool.

40
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:22,417
The incompetent will hinder
the capable without fail.

41
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:25,300
I've told you over and
over since we were kids.

42
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,980
And life is only worth
living when it has growth.

43
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:31,125
You've heard that before, too.

44
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:35,032
I've never seen wounds like those before.

45
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:38,693
What kind of attack leaves
you looking like a pincushion?

46
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:40,040
One thing's for sure.

47
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:41,614
He's hiding something.

48
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:44,140
Poor little brother. You know,

49
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:48,692
it's idiots like you who deserve to
die like a miserable roach on its back!

50
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:53,413
He's fiddling the place with tiny holes!

51
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:54,640
What is he doing?

52
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:57,040
Shining Diamond!

53
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:03,816
What kind of monster attacks
his own freakin' brother?

54
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:14,680
Josuke Higashikata.

55
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:21,160
No matter how dire the situation,
he would never abandon this brat.

56
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:24,913
I'm willing to bet he'll be
back to save him soon enough.

57
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:28,780
He'll die by my hand.

58
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:32,920
As will anyone who gets in
the way of this bow and arrow.

59
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:36,260
I'll wipe them all out of existence!

60
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:47,951
Now then, I think it's way past time
you tell me about your brother's stand.

61
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,954
What kind of power does his stand have?

62
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:55,216
Spill it and I'll get rid
of these holes in your face!

63
00:04:56,600 --> 00:05:01,240
Like I tell, I'll never rat
my bro out. Understand? Fool!

64
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:03,240
Have it your way.

65
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:05,960
I suppose.

66
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:08,880
That's just how it's gonna be.

67
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:16,977
Alright, I'm going in.

68
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:20,707
Since you're not gonna help,
just stay out of my way, Okuyasu.

69
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:24,473
Koichi doesn't have much time,
so I have to move quickly.

70
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:39,404
If earlier is any indication, his stand's
gonna attack from somewhere in the dark.

71
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:43,060
One thing's for sure, this is gonna suck.

72
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:46,100
I have to rely on instinct.

73
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:48,180
Senses don't fail me now.

74
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:49,516
Where are you going?

75
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:53,789
I gotta know, Josuke, why the
hell did you heal my injuries?

76
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:55,760
Be quiet, let me focus.

77
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:58,357
Didn't it cross your mind
that I might attack you?

78
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:00,280
I am your enemy, after all.

79
00:06:00,940 --> 00:06:01,837
Are you serious?

80
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:04,449
That depends on how
you answer my question.

81
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:06,297
Why the hell did you heal me?

82
00:06:06,380 --> 00:06:10,997
I'm having a hard time piecing things
together, so hurry up and tell me, damn it!

83
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:13,177
Also, what the hell happened to your hand?

84
00:06:13,260 --> 00:06:16,117
Did my bro do that to you when
you were pulling me out here?

85
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:18,141
None of this is making any sense.

86
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:21,554
Why'd you go through so much
trouble to try and save me?

87
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:24,408
Well, it's not complicated.

88
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:28,291
I didn't think anyone needed to die today.

89
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:30,775
Truth be told, it's as simple as that.

90
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:42,710
Koichi...

91
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:52,214
He was taken upstairs.

92
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:13,971
I'm not finished asking questions, Josuke!

93
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,737
Have you lost your goddamn mind?

94
00:07:15,820 --> 00:07:16,877
I'm trying to rescue Koichi!

95
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:17,980
I wanna know why!

96
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:22,397
Why didn't you use your stance healing
power to patch up those holes in your hand?

97
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:23,877
Instead of wrapping it like that,

98
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:27,254
you could just make it all
better, like you did my face!

99
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,477
Unfortunately, that's not how it works.

100
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:31,972
Shining Diamond can't heal my own wounds.

101
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:36,874
The fact of the matter is, life isn't
always as easy as we want it to be.

102
00:07:36,980 --> 00:07:41,940
While we're on the subject, I can't bring
back the dead no matter how hard I try.

103
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:45,480
Last thing, Okuyasu.

104
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,897
I don't know how Koichi's doing,

105
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:51,277
but if he doesn't pull through, I'm
gonna take it out on your brother.

106
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:56,242
So if shit hits the fan, be pissed off at
your bro, cause all of this is his fault.

107
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:57,830
Understand me?

108
00:07:57,913 --> 00:07:59,960
If so, go outside and wait.

109
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:18,090
Koichi!

110
00:08:18,980 --> 00:08:21,280
Shit, this has to be a trap.

111
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:24,932
He'll probably ambush me as
soon as I get close to Koichi.

112
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:26,630
But...

113
00:08:26,713 --> 00:08:29,960
Even if it is a trap, this may
be my only chance to save him!

114
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:33,694
His life is on the line, so
there's no time to hesitate!

115
00:08:36,180 --> 00:08:37,010
What?

116
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:38,900
Damn you bastard!

117
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:40,310
Yosuke!

118
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:46,460
We teleported.

119
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:49,275
I'm not the smartest guy in the world.

120
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:52,007
And I think with my
heart instead of my head.

121
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:55,536
I'll repay you for what you
did for me just this once.

122
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:57,337
That's where my gratitude ends.

123
00:08:57,420 --> 00:09:01,185
I'm not helping you out anymore,
but I won't help my bro either.

124
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:03,600
This is it.

125
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:09,960
Well, that's great to hear, Okuyasu.

126
00:09:18,980 --> 00:09:19,810
Hey!

127
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:22,257
You held up pretty great
back there, Koichi.

128
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:24,337
I'm so thrilled to see you're awake.

129
00:09:24,420 --> 00:09:26,067
How many fingers do you see?

130
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:29,510
Uh, five.

131
00:09:29,593 --> 00:09:32,697
I remember my neck being
slammed hard between the gates.

132
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,120
After that, I was...

133
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:37,280
Where the heck are we?

134
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:39,617
Sorry to have to tell you this, Koichi,

135
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:42,557
but things haven't gotten any
better while you were napping.

136
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:47,337
All I want to do right now is walk down
those stairs and leave this place behind.

137
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:51,840
But something tells me Okuyasu's
bro won't exactly comply with that.

138
00:09:59,060 --> 00:10:00,760
There's no mistaking it.

139
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:04,629
Something's lurking up there,
but it's staying out of sight.

140
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:10,190
What the?

141
00:10:10,273 --> 00:10:11,804
Something ran across that beam.

142
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:14,177
Josuke, what's going on here?

143
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:17,617
Koichi, I know you just woke up
and none of this makes sense,

144
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:20,957
but for now I need you to keep
quiet and stay close to me.

145
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:24,275
It was a hell of a lot creepier
when I couldn't see it.

146
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:26,597
Getting a look at it is actually a relief.

147
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:29,445
Looks like we've got a
pesky runt on our hands.

148
00:10:31,060 --> 00:10:33,257
As soon as that little shit shows himself,

149
00:10:33,340 --> 00:10:35,977
I'll blast him to kingdom
come with shining diamond.

150
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:39,236
Then we'll get the hell out
of here as fast as we can.

151
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:41,760
There you are!

152
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:44,050
What?

153
00:10:44,133 --> 00:10:45,017
There's a ton of those things!

154
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:47,453
And they're all in some kind of uniform!

155
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:50,080
What the...?

156
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:56,917
It's like we're being ambushed
by a bunch of toy paratroopers.

157
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,765
This is the power of
Okuyasu's brother's stand.

158
00:11:01,740 --> 00:11:02,570
Dammit!

159
00:11:02,900 --> 00:11:03,960
Son of a...

160
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:14,013
I got a few, but taking out two or
three of them isn't going to be enough.

161
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:17,960
They leave tiny wounds, but the
damage definitely packs a wallop.

162
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:21,985
If we don't play this smart, we're
going to be in major trouble.

163
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:27,980
Since my idiotic little brother decided
to meddle with my trap and save that brat,

164
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:30,437
my plan has gone off the rails somewhat.

165
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:33,317
But in the grand scheme,
it's of little consequence.

166
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:34,997
You'll never escape this house.

167
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:39,720
or the domination of my perfectly
synchronized stand, Worst Company!

168
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:53,280
So his stand is called Worst Company.

169
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:59,300
Hey, Josuke, what's
going on? Ask me later.

170
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:02,017
I know it's crazy, but
I need you to stay back.

171
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:03,237
They're up to something.

172
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:05,120
All units, halt!

173
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:08,020
Ready, aim!

174
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:10,740
Fire!

175
00:12:13,180 --> 00:12:14,640
Clare to base!

176
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:16,170
Fire!

177
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:22,580
Head on.

178
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:26,681
These little bastards have the
firepower to blow us to smithereens.

179
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:29,117
Luckily, we've got windows.

180
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:31,141
I know we're on the second floor,

181
00:12:31,260 --> 00:12:34,554
but we've got to break those
windows and jump to safety.

182
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:36,800
So much for that idea.

183
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:43,120
That's just great.

184
00:12:43,380 --> 00:12:47,657
They've even got helicopters, but how's
his stand taking the form of U .S.

185
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:49,180
Army Apache choppers?

186
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:52,441
Watch your back!

187
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:53,738
They've got a tank!

188
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:07,732
You're right, those are definitely tanks.

189
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:10,540
Koichi, careful. Wait!

190
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:13,497
Do you want to run that
by me one more time?

191
00:13:13,580 --> 00:13:15,404
Can you actually see the enemy?

192
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:18,980
The soldiers, tanks,
helicopters, all of them?

193
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:24,160
I don't understand what's
going on, but I can see them.

194
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:25,460
The arrow.

195
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:29,117
Since it didn't kill you, it
must have given you a stand.

196
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:32,020
Oh, so the Shrimp has one as well.

197
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:35,780
He's finally got the power to use a stand.

198
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:38,120
This certainly is a surprise.

199
00:13:39,180 --> 00:13:42,220
It's the man of the hour, Okuyasu's bro.

200
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:44,380
This is a pretty ballsy move.

201
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:46,661
Showing off your stand like that?

202
00:13:49,980 --> 00:13:53,820
You can think of my stand worse
company as a cast iron defense.

203
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:58,597
It renders all attacks and intruders incapable
of penetrating its protective shield.

204
00:13:58,680 --> 00:14:01,621
I know you're itching to
put me out of commission,

205
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:05,920
but sadly, it's a pipe dream
that will never come to fruition?

206
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:10,219
as your shining diamonds attacks
will never get anywhere close to me.

207
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:13,840
Feast your eyes on this.

208
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:18,560
The perfect symmetry of my army's
formation is simply stunning, isn't it?

209
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:23,300
All units, maintain
battle formation at ease!

210
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:28,597
There's just nothing quite like having
everything beautifully in place.

211
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:33,386
Though you did destroy a few of my foot
soldiers with your attack, so my troops'

212
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:36,760
formation is irritatingly
asymmetrical now. Huh.

213
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:39,017
Well, you did say you were meticulous.

214
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:42,757
But did you really need to come out of
your hiding spot to tell us all that?

215
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:45,257
Now, what on earth would
give you that idea?

216
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:48,297
I came out here to observe
the little troublemaker.

217
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:49,920
You mean me?

218
00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:50,960
Indeed I do.

219
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:53,320
If I recall, Koichi was your name.

220
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:57,517
Ironic that you appear to have the
innate ability to utilize a stand,

221
00:14:57,600 --> 00:15:01,500
Manifest your stand right now and
show me the extent of its power.

222
00:15:01,740 --> 00:15:03,380
If today's my lucky day,

223
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:07,678
you may just possess the ability
I've spent so long trying to uncover.

224
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:11,260
Show me your power and
I'll allow you to live.

225
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:13,597
But I don't know.

226
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:15,377
And what ability would that be?

227
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:18,057
It's about time you told
us what your endgame is.

228
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:20,317
I'll be asking the questions around here.

229
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:22,400
Do I make myself clear, Jazz King?

230
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:24,937
Keep in mind, I still
have you in my crosshairs.

231
00:15:25,020 --> 00:15:27,997
You should be thanking me for
letting you live as long as I have.

232
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:30,700
That's just great.
Let's go! Get a move on!

233
00:15:31,340 --> 00:15:32,516
Manifest your stand!

234
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:33,900
What's a stand?

235
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:37,000
Sorry, I have no clue what you mean. Huh?

236
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:38,395
It's your first time?

237
00:15:38,620 --> 00:15:39,780
Well, I'll be.

238
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:41,580
Very well, Josuke.

239
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:44,717
Be a sport and show him
how to manifest his stand.

240
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:45,630
What?

241
00:15:45,713 --> 00:15:49,660
The striking range of your Shining
Diamond is only a measly one meter.

242
00:15:49,980 --> 00:15:54,921
It's a long shot, but if this wimp's stand
can compensate for the weakness of yours,

243
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:58,360
You might have a real chance
at escaping my company.

244
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:00,800
Good point.

245
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:05,532
A stand that could kick your ass would
be an awesome addition to the party.

246
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:09,425
Okay, materializing your
stand is easy, Koichi.

247
00:16:09,780 --> 00:16:11,817
Ramp up the urge to protect yourself.

248
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:15,417
Or maybe think about pummeling
this guy until he's black and blue.

249
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:17,720
The rest boils down to instinct.

250
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:22,937
A stand unique to your spiritual
energy should reveal itself.

251
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:24,097
Hold on! Say what?

252
00:16:24,180 --> 00:16:25,010
What?

253
00:16:25,093 --> 00:16:27,377
You can't just bring that on me
and expect me to know what to do!

254
00:16:27,460 --> 00:16:29,160
You don't know what to do?

255
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:31,197
Then please allow me to help you out.

256
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:32,692
Here's some inspiration.

257
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:36,720
Do it, Green Beret!

258
00:16:47,420 --> 00:16:49,020
What? That's it?

259
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:05,380
Hey, Koichi, you have to try moving it.

260
00:17:05,500 --> 00:17:06,837
What are you talking about?

261
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:07,750
The stand!

262
00:17:07,833 --> 00:17:08,980
Now open your eyes!

263
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:11,190
What stand?

264
00:17:11,273 --> 00:17:13,400
Are you saying I made this thing?

265
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:15,617
Yeah, I'll congratulate you later.

266
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:18,297
First, we need to find out what
this egg-shaped thing can do.

267
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:19,262
What it can do?

268
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:22,017
I don't know what the heck you
think is supposed to happen,

269
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:23,437
but I don't have any energy left!

270
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:25,240
That was the best I could do!

271
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:26,257
You're kidding!

272
00:17:26,340 --> 00:17:28,040
That's it? Mm-hmm.

273
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:30,880
This stand.

274
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:32,950
Enough!

275
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:35,178
I've seen everything that I need to!

276
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:37,700
All units, get in battle formation!

277
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:41,060
Koichi, withdraw your stand!

278
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:43,657
If they destroy this egg, you'll die too!

279
00:17:43,740 --> 00:17:44,740
What do you mean?

280
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:46,487
I don't know how to do that!

281
00:17:46,800 --> 00:17:47,900
Light him up, men!

282
00:17:54,840 --> 00:17:55,670
Aaaaah!

283
00:17:59,940 --> 00:18:01,200
Your... Josuke!

284
00:18:02,900 --> 00:18:03,730
Excellent!

285
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,805
Those two have been separated.

286
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:08,040
The crack in that egg.

287
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:11,797
The brat doesn't realize it, but
he might have something there.

288
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:14,940
So the only man dying today is Josuke.

289
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:20,060
Word to the wise, Sergeant bro. So,

290
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:22,337
if you're trying to bring the roof of this

291
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:25,040
dump down on our heads in a fiery inferno,

292
00:18:25,260 --> 00:18:27,360
then do it and stop playing around!

293
00:18:38,980 --> 00:18:40,120
This is great.

294
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:42,700
Yeah, I'm in the mood for a brawl.

295
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:48,020
Josuke Higashikata,

296
00:18:48,280 --> 00:18:53,860
is it true that you strongly disapprove of
disparaging remarks related to your hair?

297
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:56,438
Why don't you find out for yourself?

298
00:18:56,540 --> 00:18:57,980
Go on, I dare you!

299
00:18:58,440 --> 00:19:01,205
Thanks, but I don't think
that'll be necessary.

300
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:05,557
Instead, I'll blow your head right off
from underneath that prized hair of yours!

301
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:07,346
Consider yourself forewarned!

302
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:11,320
But first-worst company will
fire bullets into your legs.

303
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:13,657
That'll keep you from running away.

304
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:16,037
Next, we'll focus on taking out your arms.

305
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:19,708
Once that's done, you'll have
no means of defending yourself.

306
00:19:19,940 --> 00:19:23,881
Giving me Card blanche to blow
your brains and hair into oblivion.

307
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:27,987
Well, that sounds like a bulletproof
plan if I ever heard one.

308
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:31,777
If you overlook the fact that
it's completely impossible...

309
00:19:31,860 --> 00:19:34,980
I've already told you how meticulous I am.

310
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:37,580
When I declare something, I stick to it.

311
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:38,839
Thus, the warning.

312
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:40,560
He's wide open.

313
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:45,115
All I have to do is make that
stand thing appear again.

314
00:19:45,620 --> 00:19:46,780
It's only an egg,

315
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:50,757
but if I can somehow hurl it
at him and make a direct hit?

316
00:19:50,840 --> 00:19:52,487
I might be able to beat him.

317
00:19:52,780 --> 00:19:55,720
All right, Koichi, time
to rise to the occasion.

318
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:58,240
I'm gonna beat him.

319
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:01,170
Remember,

320
00:20:01,253 --> 00:20:02,817
the only reason I'm still letting you draw

321
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:05,371
breath is because your stand intrigues me.

322
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:07,630
Bastard.

323
00:20:07,713 --> 00:20:10,160
All units aim, fire at will.

324
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:18,540
Hey, Sergeant Bro,

325
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,677
have you ever heard the
story where Moses parts

326
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:23,177
the waters of the Red Sea
right down the middle?

327
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:26,137
Because that's what I'm about
to do to your pathetic army.

328
00:20:26,220 --> 00:20:27,997
Then I'm going to beat you down.

329
00:20:28,080 --> 00:20:30,917
My plan is proceeding
exactly as I forewarned!

330
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,237
But you're too big of a fool to see it?

331
00:20:33,320 --> 00:20:34,720
Josuke Higashikata.

332
00:20:39,300 --> 00:20:40,260
A landmine?

333
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:42,257
First, your legs will go.

334
00:20:42,340 --> 00:20:45,500
Now, Apaches, release your
firepower and disable him!

335
00:20:54,020 --> 00:20:55,620
He got my arm.

336
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:00,540
First the legs, then the arms.

337
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:02,140
Exactly as I predicted.

338
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:06,797
Hellfire is going to rain down
on you with a flurry of bullets!

339
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,717
Can those wounded arms of yours save you?

340
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:11,120
or will worse company tear you apart?

341
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:14,753
Let's find out as it fires
every missile shell and round!

342
00:21:15,080 --> 00:21:18,360
You lose, Josuke Higashikata!

343
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:20,520
All units!

344
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:24,540
Ready, aim!

345
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:32,500
And what exactly do
you think you're doing?

346
00:21:33,140 --> 00:21:35,540
Could it be you're accepting your fate?

347
00:21:37,220 --> 00:21:39,957
Or is it that you're asking
me to show you mercy?

348
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:43,797
Well, no can do.

349
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:47,460
All you nerds take him out!

350
00:21:51,540 --> 00:21:55,893
You think you've got me cornered, but
I've already implemented my tactics.

351
00:21:57,780 --> 00:21:58,610
What?

352
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:03,557
I'm sure those are the missiles
I shot at Josuke's arm.

353
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:05,560
He turned them against me!

354
00:22:10,780 --> 00:22:12,180
What, did you forget?

355
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:15,117
My Shining Diamond's special ability is to

356
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:17,671
repair almost anything that's been broken.

357
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,880
Really, if you're that forgetful,

358
00:22:21,100 --> 00:22:25,380
you might want to take some notes
and make sure you're meticulous.

359
00:22:51,060 --> 00:22:53,577
Any time I need to see a
face, it has closed my eyes,

360
00:22:53,660 --> 00:22:55,757
and I am checking to a
base with a crystal mind,

361
00:22:55,840 --> 00:22:58,617
a magenta feeling, check a
chapter in the face of my spine,

362
00:22:58,700 --> 00:22:59,877
straight like a chicken cherry cola.

363
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:02,497
I don't need to try to
explain, I just hold on tight.

364
00:23:02,580 --> 00:23:04,837
And if it happens again,
I'ma move so slightly.

365
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:08,517
To the arms and the lips and the face Of
the humic and the ball that I need to,

366
00:23:08,600 --> 00:23:09,430
I want to.

367
00:23:09,513 --> 00:23:11,257
Come and stand a little bit closer.

368
00:23:11,340 --> 00:23:13,537
Breathe in and get a bit higher.

369
00:23:13,620 --> 00:23:17,997
You'll never know what
hit you when I get to you.

370
00:23:18,080 --> 00:23:22,340
Ooh, I want you, I don't
know if I need you?

371
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:25,580
Ooh, I got it if I need you!

372
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:31,277
Ooh, I want you, I don't
know if I need you?

373
00:23:31,360 --> 00:23:34,520
But ooh, I'm trying to find you.
